\section*{Limitations}

\paragraph{Environment scope.} Our primary experiments use ALFWorld, with cross-environment validation on ScienceWorld. The theoretical argument is environment-agnostic, but additional environments would strengthen generality.

\paragraph{Scale coverage.} 8B experiments (Section~\ref{sec:cross_scale}) confirm both failure and fix extend across the two scales tested, but report single-seed runs due to FSDP constraints. The 1.7B factorial uses two seeds per condition. ScienceWorld results (Section~\ref{sec:cross_env}) similarly report single runs. OOD generalization shows high seed variance at 1.7B (13.4pp gap across two seeds), suggesting that episode-level training's effectiveness varies with random initialization even when both seeds learn successfully.

\paragraph{Fix generality.} Cross-environment validation confirms the collapse mechanism generalizes to ScienceWorld, but the episode-level fix's effectiveness may be environment-dependent. Environments with longer episodes and more complex action spaces may require additional mechanisms beyond episode-level credit assignment.

\paragraph{Coarse episode-level credit.} For very long episodes ($T > 100$) or tasks with many independent sub-goals, uniform advantage may limit efficiency even though it preserves direction correctness.

