\subsection{Cross-Scale Verification}
\label{sec:cross_scale}

We replicate key conditions on Qwen3-8B. The 8B SFT baseline achieves 68.75\% in-distribution ($T{=}0$) and 80.6\% OOD ($T{=}0.4$). Restricting to $h{=}2$ drops in-distribution success to 31.25\% (37.5pp gap), confirming information loss extends to 8B. Cell~A collapses within two steps (28.1\% $\to$ 1.5\%). Cell~D reaches 96.9\% in-distribution and 90.3\% OOD at step~10, exceeding the SFT baseline by 9.7pp. Both failure and fix extend across the two scales tested (Table~\ref{tab:8b_results}). Single-seed due to FSDP constraints.

